=2 Walkthrough
There are 2 distinct paths to this mission and they can be done in either order.
=3 Emerald Waters (San d'Oria Path)
!Jugner Forest.jpg|right|Jugner Forest
!Carpenters Landing-map1.jpg|right|Carpenters' Landing
=5 Vicissitudes
* Zone into {z:Northern San d'Oria} for a cutscene.
* Head to the Cathedral and speak with {n:Arnau} at the altar (M-6).
** **(Optional)** Speak to him again for some lore about the former papsque.
* Speak with {n:Chasalvige}, who is in the Cathedral's Manuscript room (L-6) for a cutscene.

=5 Descendants of a Line Lost
* Head to {z:Carpenters' Landing} via the (E-6) entrance in {z:Jugner Forest}.
* Speak with {n:Guilloud} at (H-10) to spawn the NM {m:Overgrown Ivy}.
** This is a {p:Morbol}-type mob and can use {p:Hundred Fists}. You may need some high level help to defeat it if you are lower leveled.
* Speak with {n:Guilloud} again after defeating {m:Overgrown Ivy}.

=5 Louverance
* Speak with {n:Hinaree} at (B-6) in {z:Southern San d'Oria} upstairs in the Count's Manor for a cutscene to complete the San d'Oria path.

=3 Memories of a Maiden (Windurst Path)
!Attohwa Chasm-map-Remapster-maze.png|right|Attohwa Chasm
=5 Comedy Of Errors, (Act I)
* Zone into {z:Windurst Waters} for a cutscene.
* Speak to {n:Ohbiru-Dohbiru} at (J-9) inside the {p:Rhinostery}, located in South {z:Windurst Waters} (Map 2), Home Point #3 will take you right next to it.
* Speak with {p:Yoran-Oran} at (E-5) in {z:Windurst Walls} (Home Point #1).
** Yoran-Oran offers other quests unrelated to this mission so you may need to speak with him multiple times to get the right cutscene.
* Speak with {n:Kyume-Romeh} at (F-10) in {z:Windurst Waters}. He is in the Tavern. Home Point #4 will take you near it.

=5 Comedy of Errors, (Act II)
* Head to {z:Windurst Waters} (South Map Home Point #3) and speak with {n:Honoi-Gomoi} at (E-7). They are upstairs behind the house to receive the {@k}{k:Cracked Mimeo Mirror}.
* Head back to {z:Windurst Walls} (Home Point #1) and speak with {p:Yoran-Oran} (E-5) again.
* Travel to (K-8) in {z:Attohwa Chasm} and look for a spot marked as "**Loose Sand**".
** Fastest way to the {z:Chasm|Attohwa Chasm} is to use {p:Unity Warp} level 125.
** **It is recommended** to start/complete the quest {q:Middle Lands Investigation|Middle Lands Investigation|Middle Lands Investigation} before going to {z:Attohwa Chasm}. This way, you can interact with the {p:Geomagnetic Fount} for easy access to the top of {p:Parradamo Tor} without having to climb up the mountain again. However, this won't let you skip climbing the mountain again for cases like the {@k} {p:Mimeo Jewel} which will shatter upon zoning.
* To reach the **Loose Sand** you'll have to walk around the perimeter of {p:Parradamo Tor}: Start north, proceed north-east, then south until you reach (L-8).
** From (L-8), walk briefly west to reach (K-8) and the __"Loose Sand"__. It is in a dead-end underneath some fancy Attohwa trees.
* Clicking the **Loose Sand** spawns a level 51 NM {m:Antlion} named {m:Lioumere}.
** The spawning player will be hit with {@g:Physical Damage|Physical} Pit Ambush upon spawning.
** Half of Lioumere's TP moves are physical while the sand named ones are {@g:Element: Earth|Earth} **{c=#C68000:Earth}**, and it is weakest to {@g:Element: Wind|Wind} **{c=#00C900:Wind}** and {@g:Element: Light|Light} **{c=gray:Light}**.
** After Lioumere uses a TP move (like Sandblast or Sandtrap), it will return to the __Loose Sand__ and recover all its HP. So it is recommended to pull it away from the Loose Sand after spawning.
** {s:Sleep}, {s:Bind}, {s:Stun}, {s:Gravity} and a multitude of other {p:Enfeebles|Status Effects} will land and help prevent it from returning to the __Loose Sand__.
* **Read the following four points after defeating the NM, but before clicking on the Loose Sand a second time:**

+ You will receive a {@k} {p:Mimeo Jewel} after clicking the **Loose Sand** targetable location.
+ You will have exactly 30 Earth minutes to climb to the top of {p:Parradamo Tor} and reach the **Cradle of Rebirth** before the {@k} {p:Mimeo Jewel} breaks.
+ The {p:Jewel|Mimeo Jewel} will also **IMMEDIATELY BREAK** upon using a {p:Mount}, zoning, disconnecting, or using a {i:Nexus Cape|Nexus Cape|11538} while in same area, as it counts as zoning.
+ If the {p:Jewel|Mimeo Jewel} breaks, you will need to return to the **Loose Sand** and obtain another {@k} {p:Mimeo Jewel}. You will not have to re-fight the NM.

:* This can be quite frustrating for a lot of players because the path to the top is not clearly defined and falling off may mean 30 minutes or more of lost progress.

=5 Parradamo Tor
* After reading the points above, stand directly on top of the **Loose Sand** to obtain your {@k} {p:Mimeo Jewel}.
* Make your way up {p:Parradamo Tor}.
** See the **{p:Parradamo Tor}** page for help climbing the mountain.
*** Keep your camera facing the mountain and go slow, rather than wasting time falling down and starting over.
* To reach the base of the mountain at (K-9), turn around from the **Loose Sand** and proceed south-east to then hug the right wall while proceeding north-west. The base is actually rather close after all that prior running to the **Loose Sand**.
** After the base comes within view proceed south-west, behind the rock is the ramp to the path upwards.
* Once you reach the top with your {p:Jewel|Mimeo Jewel} (and sanity!) intact, check the **Cradle of Rebirth** to obtain 3 Key Items: {@k} {k:Mimeo Feather}, {@k} {k:Second Mimeo Feather}, and {@k} {k:Third Mimeo Feather}.
* Before leaving, if you have started the quest {q:Middle Lands Investigation|Middle Lands Investigation|Middle Lands Investigation} (part of a questline that unlocks {p:Proto-Waypoints|Proto-Waypoint}), go northwest of the **Cradle of Rebirth** (around where you finished your climb) to interact with the {p:Geomagnetic Fount}, so that you may teleport back to this peak anytime.

=5 Exit Stage Left
* **(Optional)** Report to {n:Kyume-Romeh} at (F-10) in {z:Windurst Waters}.
* Return to {p:Yoran-Oran} at (E-5) in {z:Windurst Walls} (Home Point #1) once again.
* Speak with {n:Yujuju} at (M-6) in {z:Port Windurst} (Home Point #3, near the Air Travel Agency)
* Head inside the eastern half of the {p:Optistery} in {z:Windurst Waters} (North map, Home Point #1) to speak with {n:Tosuka-Porika} at (G-8).
* Head back and talk to {p:Yoran-Oran} at (E-5) in {z:Windurst Walls} (Home Point #1) one final time to complete the Windurst path.
* **(Optional)** Speak to Yoran-Oran again for some additional lore about {n:Karaha-Baruha}.

----
=3 After completing both paths
* Head to the {z:Metalworks} (Home Point #1) and talk to {p:Cid} to complete the mission.

=3 Optional (Metalworks)
* The following is Unrelated to future missions, and does not need to be completed to progress.
* {q:Teak Me to the Stars|Teak Me to the Stars|Teak Me to the Stars}, part 1 of a quest chain, must be completed before {q:Hyper Active|Hyper Active|Hyper Active}. (Level 40+)
* {q:Hyper Active|Hyper Active|Hyper Active} is now available. __(verification needed)__ (Level 50+)

=3 Optional (Southern San d'Oria)
